      "content": "While populist rhetoric often exaggerates or frames issues dramatically, the core anxieties they target are frequently rooted in real systemic changes. There is genuine public discourse regarding the influence of financial systems or the pressures within educational curricula. Populists capitalize on the *feeling* of institutional overreach or hidden agendas, making tangible grievances feel like evidence of a grand conspiracy. They give voice to deep-seated skepticism about established power structures that traditional media often overlooks in favor of consensus narrative.",
